\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {S7}{\ignorespaces Pairwise MI preservation across all eight Pfam families. Each bar shows the Pearson correlation between the upper-triangle MI vector of the stored seed alignment and the MI vector of sequences generated by the indicated method. The general ordering HMM $<$ SA gen $<$ Potts $\leq $ EvoDiff reflects the information hierarchy of each model in several families, though Defensin\_beta is an exception where the Potts model ($r{=}0.23$) falls below both SA and HMM. Pkinase is an outlier for SA, HMM, and MSAT owing to its high data-to-position ratio ($K{=}37$, $L{=}262$), while Potts and EvoDiff achieve high MI correlations on this family.}}{8}{figure.caption.14}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:mi-barplot}{{S7}{8}{Pairwise MI preservation across all eight Pfam families. Each bar shows the Pearson correlation between the upper-triangle MI vector of the stored seed alignment and the MI vector of sequences generated by the indicated method. The general ordering HMM $<$ SA gen $<$ Potts $\leq $ EvoDiff reflects the information hierarchy of each model in several families, though Defensin\_beta is an exception where the Potts model ($r{=}0.23$) falls below both SA and HMM. Pkinase is an outlier for SA, HMM, and MSAT owing to its high data-to-position ratio ($K{=}37$, $L{=}262$), while Potts and EvoDiff achieve high MI correlations on this family}{figure.caption.14}{}}
